/-
The Kähler module of a valuation subring, generated by the uniformiser's differential.

For a place `v` of `F` over `K`, the differential `D π` of a uniformiser of the valuation
subring `𝒪ᵥ` spans `Ω[𝒪ᵥ⁄K]` — the input the canonical-divisor construction consumes.
The proof is a chain of `Prop`-valued model predicates about the map `K[X] → 𝒪ᵥ` that
sends `X` to the uniformiser (`Place.polynomialAlgebra`):

* `ValSubringPolynomialFormallyUnramified`: the Kähler module of `𝒪ᵥ` over `K[X]`
  vanishes, i.e. `K[X] → 𝒪ᵥ` is formally unramified — enough for the span to be everything;
* `ValSubringKaehlerFinite`: `Ω[𝒪ᵥ⁄K]` is a finite module, and with separable residue
  field degrees over `K` this gives formal unramifiedness back;
* `ValSubringEssFiniteType` / `ValSubringFiniteTypeModel`: `𝒪ᵥ` is essentially of finite
  type over `K`, resp. a localisation of a finite-type `K`-subalgebra;
* `ValSubringDedekindModel` / `ValSubringDedekindFractionModel`: `𝒪ᵥ` is the localisation
  of the integral closure of a Dedekind model at the centre ideal of `v`.

Each section is one implication of the chain, ending in
`valSubringKaehlerSpanTop_of_polynomialFormallyUnramified` and its converse direction
`valSubringDedekindModel_of_dedekindFractionModel`. `ValuationSubring`'s generic
`idealOfLE` facts and the centre-ideal localisation machinery are the algebra the
Dedekind step needs.

After FLT's `P2M/Sol/S_AlgebraicCurve_hasCanonicalDivisor_of_isCurveOver.lean`
(1,723 ln, first half), pinned at `aa2d8b3`: <https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b3/P2M/Sol/S_AlgebraicCurve_hasCanonicalDivisor_of_isCurveOver.lean>.

Assumes: `Place.uniformizer` / `Place.uniformizerSubring` (`Defs/CanonicalDivisor.lean`),
the Kähler dictionary of `Defs/KaehlerTranscendental.lean` and `Defs/PlacesOverDVR.lean`,
and `Place.mem_vs_of_ord_nonneg` / `Place.ord_nonneg_of_mem_vs`.

spec-pin: P2M/Sol/S_AlgebraicCurve_hasCanonicalDivisor_of_isCurveOver.lean
-/
